  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q40-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{x-3}$ and $g(x)=\\frac{x-2}{x+1}$. Find the value of the variable in each of the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p15-q40-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(4)=g(a)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p15-q40-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a=-\\frac{7}{4}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p15-q40-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{a-2}{a+1}=5",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and clear the denominator.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$a\\ne-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(4)&=\\frac{4+1}{4-3}\\\\f(4)&=5\\\\\\frac{a-2}{a+1}&=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $\\frac{A}{B}=\\frac{C}{D}$ with $B,D\\ne0$, multiplying both sides by $BD$ gives $AD=BC$. Here multiply by $a+1$ and distribute the $5$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a-2&=5a+5\\\\-4a&=7\\\\a&=-\\frac{7}{4}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis value is allowed: $a+1=-\\frac{3}{4}\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q40-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(b)=g(1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p15-q40-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "b=\\frac{1}{3}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p15-q40-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{b+1}{b-3}=-\\frac{1}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and clear the denominators.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$b\\ne3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}g(1)&=\\frac{1-2}{1+1}\\\\g(1)&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\\\\\frac{b+1}{b-3}&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $b-3\\ne0$, multiply both sides by $2(b-3)$, then distribute and collect like terms.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2(b+1)&=-(b-3)\\\\2b+2&=-b+3\\\\3b&=1\\\\b&=\\frac{1}{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis value is allowed: $b-3=-\\frac{8}{3}\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q40-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(c)=g(c)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p15-q40-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "c=\\frac{5}{7}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p15-q40-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Clear denominators and expand to obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "7c=5",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$c\\ne3,-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{c+1}{c-3}&=\\frac{c-2}{c+1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth denominators are nonzero, so multiply both sides by $(c-3)(c+1)$. Expand by multiplying every term in one bracket by every term in the other, then collect like terms.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(c+1)^2&=(c-2)(c-3)\\\\c^2+2c+1&=c^2-5c+6\\\\7c&=5\\\\c&=\\frac{5}{7}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis value is allowed: $c-3=-\\frac{16}{7}\\ne0$ and $c+1=\\frac{12}{7}\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q40-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(2d)=g(d)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p15-q40-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "d=\\frac{1}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p15-q40-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Clear denominators and expand to obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "10d=5",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$d\\ne\\frac{3}{2},-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2d+1}{2d-3}&=\\frac{d-2}{d+1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth denominators are nonzero, so multiply both sides by $(2d-3)(d+1)$. Expand by multiplying every term in one bracket by every term in the other, then collect like terms.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(2d+1)(d+1)&=(d-2)(2d-3)\\\\2d^2+3d+1&=2d^2-7d+6\\\\10d&=5\\\\d&=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis value is allowed: $2d-3=-2\\ne0$ and $d+1=\\frac{3}{2}\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
